WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.964 --> 00:00:06.276
In this tutorial, we'll make a complete short film with LocalFlow: from a

2
00:00:06.276 --> 00:00:11.806
two-sentence idea to a finished video, with keyframes, motion, voices, sound

3
00:00:11.806 --> 00:00:13.189
effects, and music.

4
00:00:13.189 --> 00:00:17.426
Apart from the story writing, everything runs on your own GPU.

5
00:00:18.082 --> 00:00:20.557
Start with a new project, and give it a name.

6
00:00:25.607 --> 00:00:28.519
Write the idea, and set a target length.

7
00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:33.557
Fifteen seconds gives us a few shots: enough to see the whole pipeline.

8
00:00:34.126 --> 00:00:39.865
Now refine the idea into a story, build the story bible, and break it down into

9
00:00:39.865 --> 00:00:40.301
shots.

10
00:00:40.301 --> 00:00:44.051
Your language model takes a few seconds for each step.

11
00:01:00.729 --> 00:01:06.360
We have scenes and shots, each sized to fit one video clip, and an ingredient for

12
00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.654
every character, place, and prop.

13
00:01:11.238 --> 00:01:13.613
Next, give the main character a look.

14
00:01:13.613 --> 00:01:18.226
On the Ingredients tab, pick the FLUX dev model, and click Generate.

15
00:01:26.369 --> 00:01:30.032
The first candidate becomes the character's primary reference.

16
00:01:30.032 --> 00:01:34.530
The other characters, places, and props get theirs the same way, so let's

17
00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.132
fast-forward through them.

18
00:01:46.697 --> 00:01:47.934
Now the big step.

19
00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:53.517
On the Shots board, Generate all composes a keyframe for every shot from its

20
00:01:53.517 --> 00:01:57.409
references, then animates each keyframe with Wan 2.2.

21
00:01:57.409 --> 00:02:02.663
With Use each new keyframe right away ticked, it runs from start to finish on its

22
00:02:02.663 --> 00:02:02.922
own.

23
00:02:10.149 --> 00:02:14.524
This is the longest part: a few minutes of GPU time per shot.

24
00:02:14.524 --> 00:02:16.799
You can keep working, or step away.

25
00:02:16.799 --> 00:02:18.962
Progress shows in the Jobs drawer.

26
00:02:28.751 --> 00:02:32.189
Every shot now has a keyframe and a video take.

27
00:02:32.189 --> 00:02:33.589
Open a shot to see them.

28
00:02:37.491 --> 00:02:43.241
Check consistency asks a vision model to compare the take with the reference images.

29
00:02:43.241 --> 00:02:47.837
It lists anything that drifted, like a different hair color, and suggests a

30
00:02:47.837 --> 00:02:48.879
corrected prompt.

31
00:02:55.028 --> 00:02:57.716
Here's the verdict, with anything that drifted.

32
00:02:57.716 --> 00:03:02.478
Apply fix puts the corrected prompt into the shot, ready to regenerate.

33
00:03:05.344 --> 00:03:08.006
Below the video is the Audio section.

34
00:03:08.006 --> 00:03:13.575
Generate dialogue speaks the shot's lines in each character's voice, timed to the

35
00:03:13.575 --> 00:03:13.919
clip.

36
00:03:13.919 --> 00:03:19.344
Generate sound effects watches the picture, and makes matching sound with MMAudio.

37
00:03:24.774 --> 00:03:27.449
The other shots get their audio the same way.

38
00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:38.351
On the Timeline tab, Auto-assemble lays out every take in order, with its dialogue

39
00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.687
and sound effects on their own tracks.

40
00:03:41.265 --> 00:03:42.952
Press play to preview the cut.

41
00:03:42.952 --> 00:03:47.415
You can trim clips, reorder them, and change the transitions right here.

42
00:03:49.084 --> 00:03:51.796
For a score, click plus on the Music track.

43
00:03:51.796 --> 00:03:57.126
MusicGen composes from the shots' music cues, and the result is placed under the

44
00:03:57.126 --> 00:03:57.859
whole film.

45
00:04:06.767 --> 00:04:08.492
Finally, export.

46
00:04:08.492 --> 00:04:14.317
Pick a size, and LocalFlow renders an MP4 with every track mixed together.

47
00:04:16.935 --> 00:04:18.135
And here's our film.

48
00:04:39.012 --> 00:04:41.549
Everything you made is in the Assets tab.

49
00:04:41.549 --> 00:04:46.850
Filter by type, model, or scene, group things into collections, or reuse any

50
00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.362
result's settings in the Playground.

51
00:04:50.861 --> 00:04:56.061
That's the whole journey, from an idea to a finished film, on your own machine.

52
00:04:56.061 --> 00:04:59.411
The other tutorials go deeper into each step.
